-- title:
--   Theorem 2.4 — primal convergence rates of Frank-Wolfe under the step-size rules (i), (i'), (ii), (iii)
-- statement:
--   Under Assumption 2.3, every sequence $(x_t)$ generated by the Frank-Wolfe algorithm satisfies, for all $t\ge1$,
--   $$
--   f(x_t)-\min_{\mathcal C}f\le\begin{cases}L(\operatorname{diam}\mathcal C)^2(1+\ln t)/(2t)&\text{if $(\gamma_t)$ follows (i);}\\ 2L(\operatorname{diam}\mathcal C)^2/(t+2)&\text{if $(\gamma_t)$ follows (i');}\\ 4L(\operatorname{diam}\mathcal C)^2/(t+2)&\text{if $(\gamma_t)$ follows (ii);}\\ 4L(\operatorname{diam}\mathcal C)^2/(t+2)&\text{if $(\gamma_t)$ follows (iii).}\end{cases}
--   $$
--   Here $\min_{\mathcal C}f$ is the minimum of $f$ over $\mathcal C$, and the bound holds for every oracle selection and every admissible step (Remark 2.2(i)).
--
--   These are the classical rates that the paper's counterexamples respect: the function values converge although the iterates need not. Related results on the platform (`JaggiFW.PrimalDual.theorem_1`, `ConvexOptAlg.FrankWolfe.theorem_3_8`) use other constants, step sizes or a global $C^1$ hypothesis, so this item is posed afresh.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--
--   - encoding: min_C f → any m with IsLeast (f '' C) m; reason: the minimum exists (C compact, f continuous on C) and is unique
--   - encoding: "the Frank-Wolfe algorithm satisfies" → every sequence x with IsFWRun C f rule x₀ x, for every x₀ ∈ C; reason: Remark 2.2(i) defines the generated sequences; every oracle selection is covered
--   - encoding: rule (ii) at x_t = v_t, where the quotient is 0/0 → γ_t = 0 (Lean's 0/0 = 0); reason: every γ_t gives the same x_{t+1} = x_t, so no sequence changes
--   - encoding: f : D → ℝ → f : ℝⁿ → ℝ with every property (convexity, differentiability, gradient) required on D only; reason: the values of f outside D never enter; D is open, so gradients at points of D are the true ones
--   - encoding: ℝⁿ, diam C → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n), Metric.diam C; reason: the same space and diameter (C is bounded)
-- source:
--   Bolte, Combettes & Pauwels, The Iterates of the Frank-Wolfe Algorithm May Not Converge, arXiv:2202.08711v1, Theorem 2.4, p.4 (quoted from [23, 10, 16])

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FWIterates_Assumption23
import Definitions.Def_FWIterates_IsFWRun

open scoped RealInnerProductSpace

namespace FWIterates

/-- **Theorem 2.4** (arXiv:2202.08711v1, Theorem 2.4, p.4, quoted from [23, 10, 16]). Under
Assumption 2.3, every sequence generated by the Frank-Wolfe algorithm satisfies, for all `t ≥ 1`,
`f(xₜ) − min_C f ≤ L(diam C)²(1 + ln t)/(2t)` with rule (i), `≤ 2L(diam C)²/(t + 2)` with rule (i'),
and `≤ 4L(diam C)²/(t + 2)` with rule (ii) and with rule (iii).

**Formalization Note** `min_C f` is any `m` with `IsLeast (f '' C) m` (it exists because `C` is
compact and `f` continuous on `C`). `diam C` is `Metric.diam C`. The rule (ii) uses the constant
`L` of Assumption 2.3. Every oracle selection and every admissible step is covered (`IsFWRun`). -/
theorem theorem_2_4 {n : ℕ} {C D : Set (EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n))}
    {f : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n) → ℝ} {L : ℝ} (hA : Assumption23 C D f L) {m : ℝ}
    (hm : IsLeast (f '' C) m) (x₀ : EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin n)) :
    (∀ x, IsFWRun C f (openLoop n) x₀ x → ∀ t : ℕ, 1 ≤ t →
        f (x t) - m ≤ L * Metric.diam C ^ 2 * (1 + Real.log t) / (2 * t)) ∧
    (∀ x, IsFWRun C f (openLoop' n) x₀ x → ∀ t : ℕ, 1 ≤ t →
        f (x t) - m ≤ 2 * L * Metric.diam C ^ 2 / ((t : ℝ) + 2)) ∧
    (∀ x, IsFWRun C f (closedLoop f L) x₀ x → ∀ t : ℕ, 1 ≤ t →
        f (x t) - m ≤ 4 * L * Metric.diam C ^ 2 / ((t : ℝ) + 2)) ∧
    (∀ x, IsFWRun C f (lineSearch f) x₀ x → ∀ t : ℕ, 1 ≤ t →
        f (x t) - m ≤ 4 * L * Metric.diam C ^ 2 / ((t : ℝ) + 2)) := by sorry

end FWIterates
